"md": "**【If you're at this wall】**\n\nYou did it.\n\nYou go to pray and that scene comes up. Standing in front of God is uncomfortable.\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 1】**\n\n**[Bible · Genesis 3:8-10](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/GEN.3.8-10.ESV)**\n\n**[Bible · Luke 15:20](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/LUK.15.20.ESV)**\n\nLook at what the first human beings did.\n\nAfter they sinned, they heard God's voice — and hid among the trees.\n\nGod called out, \"Where are you?\" He was looking for them.\n\nAnd Adam answered: **I was afraid, because I was naked, and I hid myself.**\n\n**When they sinned, they hid.**\n\nIt's the same now. When we do something, we stop praying. We stop opening the Bible. We drift away from church.\n\n**God didn't move away. We're the ones hiding.**\n\nAnd remember the father of the prodigal son. **While he was still a long way off, he ran to him.**\n\nNow that Jesus has settled sin at the cross, if you do sin, **you can run into his grace, full of gratitude for being forgiven.**\n\n**God is the one who comes looking. There's no reason to hide.**\n\n- What am I hiding from God right now?\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 2】**\n\n**[Bible · Matthew 27:50-51](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/MAT.27.50-51.ESV)**\n\n**[Bible · Hebrews 10:19-22](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/HEB.10.19-22.ESV)**\n\nThe moment Jesus breathed his last on the cross, the curtain of the temple was torn in two, from top to bottom.\n\nThat curtain hid the innermost place where God was. Thick fabric. Nobody could go in — except one man, once a year.\n\nAnd it tore from top to bottom.\n\n**A human didn't rip it open from below. It was torn from above.**\n\nGod opened it with his own hands. And it's stayed open.\n\nSo the Bible says: **we have confidence to enter the holy places.**\n\n**We don't need to politely close a door God opened.**\n\n- \"It's already open.\" What happened in you when you read that?\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 3】**\n\n**[Bible · 1 John 1:9](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/1JN.1.9.ESV)**\n\n**[Bible · Romans 8:1](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/ROM.8.1.ESV)**\n\n**[Bible · Romans 6:6-11](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/ROM.6.6-11.ESV)**\n\nThe Bible says: **If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.**\n\n\"Confess\" here means, in the original, saying the same thing God says.\n\nWhat God calls sin, you call sin too. No fudging.\n\nAnd God is saying something else as well: that sin has already been handled by the blood.\n\n**So we say the same thing.**\n\nYou don't need to repeat \"I'm sorry\" over and over to earn forgiveness. Forgiveness is already paid for. Go all the way to \"Thank you — I'm already washed.\"\n\nAnd the Bible says: **There is therefore now no condemnation for those who are in Jesus the Savior.**\n\n**No condemnation.**\n\nIt goes on: **our old self was crucified with Jesus.** And, **consider yourselves dead to sin and alive to God.**\n\n**Sinning isn't what we actually are anymore.**\n\nThe old nature died. We were born into a new one. If you've sinned, what happened is that you did something that isn't you anymore.\n\nSo don't stay there. Come straight back.\n\n**And here's what matters.**\n\nLearn to tell the condemning voice from the correcting one.\n\nGod's correction points somewhere. It says, \"Come back here.\"\nA condemning voice stops you. It ends at \"You're a failure.\"\n\n**If it condemns and stops there, it isn't God.**\n\n**Guilt isn't a sign to move away from God. It's a sign to come straight back.**\n\n- What's stopping me right now — a voice that points, or a voice that condemns?\n\n---\n\n**【Try this】**\n\n**① Say it plainly**\n> \"Today I did ______.\"\n\nNo fudging. God already knows.\n\n**② Receive it**\n> \"Jesus, thank you for washing this away with your blood. Because of that I'm completely clean. Thank you for the power never to sin again. I died to sin and I came alive through your life.\"\n\n**③ Talk to him right there, exactly like normal**\n\nThis is the most important one.\n\n**What breaks closeness isn't sin. It's the silence after sin.**\n\nDon't end the day with it still awkward. Come straight back.\n\n**Awkwardness isn't a reason to move away from God. It's a reason to come closer.**\n\n---\n\n**And if it keeps happening.**\n\nIf it's the same thing over and over, stop fighting it alone.\n\nThe Bible says: **Confess your sins to one another and pray for one another, that you may be healed.**\n\nTell a leader, or a brother or sister of the same gender you trust. What stays hidden gets stronger. What gets brought into the light loses its grip.\n\nAnd use【Taste】. If you've sinned and can't face him, that's exactly when to take the bread and the cup. Receive what was paid, with your body.\n\n---\n\n**【One line to God】**（prayer）\n\nUse your own words.\n\n> （example）\"I was hiding. Sorry. But you're the one who comes looking. I'm coming back.\"\n\n---\n\n**【One line for today】**\n\nWhat I thought about today.\n＿＿＿＿＿＿"
