"md": "**【If you're at this wall】**\n\nYou want to. And then the day is over.\n\n**Time with God ends up last in line.**\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 1】**\n\n**[Bible · Luke 10:38-42](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/LUK.10.38-42.ESV)**\n\nMartha was working to host Jesus. She did nothing wrong.\n\nThe Bible says: **Martha was distracted with much serving.**\n\nAnd she protested: **\"Do you not care that my sister has left me to serve alone?\"**\n\nJesus answered: **\"Martha, Martha, you are anxious and troubled about many things, but one thing is necessary.\"**\n\n**One thing is necessary.**\n\nMartha's failure wasn't laziness. She worked so hard for Jesus that she lost Jesus himself.\n\n- What am I spending the most time on right now, and what is it for?\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 2】**\n\n**[Bible · Mark 1:32-35](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/MRK.1.32-35.ESV)**\n\nLook at Jesus' day.\n\nIn the evening, the whole town brought their sick. The whole city was gathered together at the door. He healed many.\n\nAnd the next morning. Rising very early, while it was still dark, he departed to a desolate place, and there he prayed.\n\n**The busiest person in the world made time to be alone.**\n\nAnd right after this, the disciples come looking for him. **\"Everyone is looking for you.\"**\n\nThe demand was infinite. He still went alone first.\n\nThink about it. The Son of God needed time to pray.\n\nWhere does that leave \"I don't have time\"?\n\n- When is the quietest, least interrupted hour of my day?\n\n---\n\n**【Taste 3】**\n\n**[Bible · Matthew 6:33](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/MAT.6.33.ESV)**\n\n**[Bible · Psalm 90:12](https://www.bible.com/bible/59/PSA.90.12.ESV)**\n\nJesus said: **Seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness, and all these things will be added to you.**\n\n**First.**\n\nIt's about order. Not if there's time left over. You put it at the front.\n\nSame structure as giving the firstfruits.（Covered in detail in【Put God first】) Giving what's left means \"I'll treasure this if I have margin.\" Giving what's first means \"I treasure this before anything else.\"\n\nTime works the same way.\n\nAnd Moses prayed: Teach us to number our days that we may get a heart of wisdom.\n\n**Time is finite.**\n\nSo \"I don't have time\" usually isn't accurate. Everyone has twenty-four hours. It isn't that there's not enough — it's that other things went in first.\n\n**We try to secure time for what we actually think matters.** So how you use your time right now **shows you the direction of your heart.**\n\nThat might sound harsh. But it's good news.\n\nIf it's a question of order, it can change. Put it first, starting today.\n\n**It isn't that you have no time. The order is off.**\n\n**Busyness isn't a sign you've drifted from God. It's a sign to put the order back.**\n\n- If I put time with God first, how would my day change?\n\n---\n\n**【Try this】**\n\n**① Start with 5 minutes**\nDon't wait for a free hour. Five minutes.\nFive minutes daily goes deeper than three hours once a month.\n\n**② Set a time and put it in the calendar**\n\"When I have a gap\" never arrives. Decide the hour and put it in.\nMorning, commute, before bed — anywhere.\n\n**③ Stop one thing**\nNew time has to come from somewhere.\n**What's the one thing you'll stop today?** Phone, video, social media. **Use【Cut】.**\n\n---\n\n**And hold on to this.**\n\n**Busyness isn't bad.**\n\nThe problem isn't busyness. It's God ending up at the back of the line inside it.\n\nYou can talk to him all day, like someone sitting next to you. On the train, over the dishes, three minutes before bed.\n\nThere are seasons where nobody can find a block of time. The people who stay connected in scraps during those seasons come out the deepest on the other side.\n\n---\n\n**【One line to God】**（prayer）\n\nUse your own words.\n\n> （example）\"I kept saying I had no time. You ended up last. Starting today you go first.\"\n\n---\n\n**【One line for today】**\n\nWhat I thought about today.\n＿＿＿＿＿＿"
